# Read state first (all agents, every session)

The system (spine, CC, PE, SmartCity, engines) is too large to hold in one context. Drift happens when a fresh agent acts without the standing decisions and current state. Before doing ANY substantive work:

1. READ `_STATE.md` — the living "where we are right now": the one-line status, STANDING DECISIONS (govern everything), LIVE INFRA (serving revisions), what's DONE, what's OPEN, what's HELD. This is your pickup point.
2. READ `MEMORY.md` (auto-memory index) — durable rules/decisions. The top lines are load-bearing (standing-decisions-travel, Cotality-extinguished, deploys-planner-owned). Scan the whole index; open the file for any that touches your task.
3. THEN read the specific doc for your task (named in `_STATE.md` KEY DOCS).

STANDING DECISIONS you must not violate (full list in `_STATE.md`):
- Cotality is EXTINGUISHED — re-route, never rotate its credential.
- Deploys are planner-owned — never escalate a deploy to the operator.
- No privileged data access — uniform public-record only.
- CTX / national is HELD until Bastrop QA-done + operator go.
- Code-done != customer-done — a grade is a live probe on the deployed surface, never a merged PR.

When you finish or hand off: UPDATE `_STATE.md` (its OPEN and LIVE INFRA sections) so the next agent picks up from truth, not from a stale doc. If you made a durable decision or hit a reusable lesson, flag it for promotion to memory (do not self-promote; the planner gates it — see fleet-memory rule).

Do not assume you know the current state from an earlier session or from the task prompt alone. State changes constantly. `_STATE.md` is the truth; read it first.
